  "notes": [
    "orders come from self-convergence on a fixed grid, so every dt-independent (spatial) error cancels in the difference",
    "pressure is compared after removing its spatial mean: the projection potential is defined up to an additive constant",
    "the first-order control keeps the production projection and replaces only the trapezoidal momentum averaging, so it isolates the time scheme",
    "error_vs_exact is reported next to the orders on purpose: it saturates at the spatial floor and must not be read as a temporal order",
    "each grid refines dt only: the time-step series is halved per grid doubling so that dt/h, and hence the convective CFL number, is fixed"
  ],
  "cfl_note": "grids refine dt in step with h, so dt/h and the convective CFL number are held fixed; n=32 with dt=0.2 s is rejected by the Picard iteration (residual NaN) and is never reported as a result",
